# Host node_modules must never enter the build context: the builder stage does
# `COPY --from=deps /app/node_modules` and then `COPY . .`, so an un-ignored
# host tree silently overwrites the correctly-installed one. A stale host copy
# (next 16.2.11 against the pinned 16.3.3) paired 16.3.3's native swc binary
# with 16.2.11's JS and broke `pnpm build` with
# "Error: Missing field `turbopackMemoryEviction`".
node_modules/
.next/
out/
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
__tests__/
.git
.github
*.log
*.md
eslint.config*
playwright.config.ts
